  "_exec_summary": [
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000120358,
      "SummaryText": "DHL Supply Chain, Inc., is a refrigerated/frozen warehouse engaged in storing and distributing refrigerated and frozen food products to area retail outlets.  To maintain refrigerated/frozen conditions in the warehouse, DHL Supply Chain operates a mechanical refrigeration system in which the refrigerant is anhydrous ammonia.  No manufacturing is done at the site.  Products are brought to the site by truck for storage;  various assortments of these products are then assembled for reshipment to area outlets.\n\nThis refrigeration plant was newly constructed in 1997.  DHL Supply Chain  has long been committed to employee safety and to being a good community neighbor.  To this end, DHL Supply Chain maintains an active safety management program to prevent accidental releases of ammonia.  The facility complies with OSHA's PSM rule, and maintains a written Process Safety Plan onsite.\n\nA rigorous program of operator training, preventive maintenance, and periodic inspections is maintained, to prevent the accidental  release of ammonia, and all required safety programs are in force at the facility.  While the facility is a relatively new one, there have been no reportable accidental releases of ammonia since start-up, and no accidents involving the release of ammonia.  DHL Supply Chain has coordinated emergency response activities with the local (Aurora) Fire Department.  The nearest Fire Department Substation is less than two (2) miles distant.\n\nThe facility is located to the West of the City of Aurora downtown area, in a location which which is urban and industrial. The refrigeration system is d adequately for the amount of cooling needed, and is capable of holding 29,000 lbs of anhydrous ammonia.  All ammonia is stored in the system; there is no additional storage on-site.\n\nDHL Supply Chain  personnel are trained to respond to minor releases and minor repair/maintenance problems.  However, for a major release, the facility would call upon the Aurora Fire Department for emerge"
    },
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 1,
      "FacilityID": 1000120358,
      "SummaryText": "ncy response and DualTemp Companies service department.  Facility personnel are trained n response actions which consist of minimizing damage to the facility while assisting the orderly evacuation of all personnel.  DHL Supply Chain regularly evaluates and implements any appropriate measures to further improve safety."
    }
  ]
